WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:21.333 --> 00:00:25.625
Welcome to the Sept of Baylor, a shrine to bad front-office decisions, 

00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:28.666
the kind that have led all of you here to the draft lottery!

00:00:31.375 --> 00:00:34.208
Today, we gather in the presence of the lottery gods

00:00:34.208 --> 00:00:37.000
to witness the bestowing of the first pick.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:40.458
I am Mark Tatum, Hand of the High Commissioner

00:00:40.458 --> 00:00:41.416
Where’s the Silver Lord?

00:00:41.416 --> 00:00:43.291
What, he too good for us?

00:00:43.291 --> 00:00:45.000
Yes, actually. And besides, this is… 

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:47.125
Yes, actually. And besides, this is… 

00:00:47.125 --> 00:00:48.083
this is sort of my thing.

00:00:48.083 --> 00:00:48.916
Yeah, you know what?

00:00:48.916 --> 00:00:51.791
Let’s just take a moment to appreciate Mark Tatum

00:00:52.750 --> 00:00:54.250
That’s right!

00:00:54.250 --> 00:00:56.208
Let’s give a little love to the guy behind the guy

00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:58.125
OK all right. Thanks.

00:00:58.125 --> 00:01:02.958
As per tradition, each house has chosen one delegate to represent them

00:01:02.958 --> 00:01:05.250
I do question some of your delegate choices,

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:08.083
but then again, questionable decisions are why 

00:01:08.083 --> 00:01:10.708
many of you find yourselves here.

00:01:10.708 --> 00:01:12.750
Um...House Pelicans...

00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:15.958
Come on, you know who the fanlings want to see

00:01:15.958 --> 00:01:17.250
That’s better

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:19.791
Um...excuse me, House Mavs? 

00:01:19.791 --> 00:01:21.375
What is this?

00:01:21.375 --> 00:01:23.125
We’re, uh, Triple Dirks

00:01:23.125 --> 00:01:25.416
OK, well, you gotta pick one representative,

00:01:25.416 --> 00:01:28.541
so figure out who is the next Dirk in the next 10 seconds, please.

00:01:28.541 --> 00:01:31.708
All right, well, I mean, I’m the most experienced…

00:01:31.708 --> 00:01:34.291
Well, I’m clearly the face of House Mavericks

00:01:34.291 --> 00:01:36.250
And I’m from Dirk’s hometown

00:01:36.250 --> 00:01:37.666
so yeah...I mean it’s hard

00:01:37.666 --> 00:01:38.791
We all have really good cases

00:01:38.791 --> 00:01:41.333
All right, you know what? I’ll let you guys sort this out next season

00:01:41.333 --> 00:01:42.375
House Lakers?

00:01:42.375 --> 00:01:45.375
-Get out there
-All right. Get off me

00:01:46.291 --> 00:01:47.458
Hi

00:01:47.458 --> 00:01:48.375
Hey

00:01:48.375 --> 00:01:50.500
OK, so, we’re all good?

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:52.000
Everyone knows how this works?

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:54.250
Uh...not really

00:01:54.250 --> 00:01:57.000
Right. Well, each house will have a chance to make

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:59.291
their final plea to the lottery gods as to 

00:01:59.291 --> 00:02:01.875
why they should get the first pick.

00:02:01.875 --> 00:02:04.458
So, who would like to be the first to make a claim?

00:02:05.541 --> 00:02:08.708
Great, the goat...made poop on the floor

00:02:08.708 --> 00:02:09.625
Excuse me?

00:02:09.625 --> 00:02:10.500
No, not you

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:12.666
Sarver, why is there a goat here?

00:02:12.666 --> 00:02:15.500
Because it’s a metaphor and it’s FUNNY

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:18.000
OK, well, please send a new representative down

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:19.375
Preferably a human

00:02:19.375 --> 00:02:21.291
OK, the floor is open

00:02:21.291 --> 00:02:24.041
Oh...I’ll take a stab here

00:02:24.041 --> 00:02:25.750
I would say to the gods  

00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:28.958
that you should give House Kings the first pick because—

00:02:28.958 --> 00:02:31.291
Actually, no, it would go to the Sixers

00:02:31.291 --> 00:02:33.708
Aw, crap, yeah...

00:02:33.708 --> 00:02:37.291
OK, gods, you should give House Kings the second pick—

00:02:37.291 --> 00:02:40.166
No, then it would go to House Celtics, I believe

00:02:40.166 --> 00:02:43.166
Wait, what? Who made this—I made this

00:02:43.166 --> 00:02:44.166
Ugh

00:02:44.166 --> 00:02:46.875
OK, do some—someone else should go. I don’t want to.

00:02:46.875 --> 00:02:49.875
No house has fallen harder than that of the Grizzly

00:02:49.875 --> 00:02:51.750
Ser Gasol is gone,

00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:56.041
but Chandler Parsons—and his stupid contract—remain

00:02:56.041 --> 00:02:57.333
Eh, could be worse

00:02:57.333 --> 00:03:01.291
Bless us, oh lottery gods, with the squire Zion, 

00:03:01.291 --> 00:03:04.125
so that Grit and Grind may rise again,

00:03:04.125 --> 00:03:06.958
as a bane to all Western powers.

00:03:06.958 --> 00:03:10.875
The great House Knicks has not had a first pick in over 30 years

00:03:10.875 --> 00:03:12.041
Lord Fizdale?

00:03:12.041 --> 00:03:16.208
We finally have cast off our overrated European big man

00:03:16.208 --> 00:03:18.958
to make room for the Great Zion

00:03:18.958 --> 00:03:21.666
Please, gods, take that for data,

00:03:21.666 --> 00:03:24.041
and give House Knicks the first pick.

00:03:24.041 --> 00:03:24.875
Oh yeah, please

00:03:24.875 --> 00:03:26.333
If House Knicks gets Zion, they’ll just

00:03:26.333 --> 00:03:28.958
send him away in another terrible trade, right?

00:03:28.958 --> 00:03:29.583
Rude!

00:03:29.583 --> 00:03:34.458
You, Ser Kristaps, are now banned from The Garden!

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:37.500
OK, you can’t just ban an opposing knight from your arena

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:39.000
You’re banned, Mark!

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:41.291
Does anyone else want to make a plea to the gods?

00:03:41.291 --> 00:03:43.458
Ah, Ser Devin. Welcome.

00:03:43.458 --> 00:03:44.750
Screw House Suns!

00:03:44.750 --> 00:03:46.541
They rejected our alliance 

00:03:46.541 --> 00:03:48.583
and stole the first pick from us last year.

00:03:48.583 --> 00:03:49.833
Yeah, they already have Luka!

00:03:49.833 --> 00:03:50.791
No they don’t

00:03:50.791 --> 00:03:53.083
Wait, so who did you guys take?

00:03:53.083 --> 00:03:54.041
I think Trae Young

00:03:54.041 --> 00:03:55.541
Huh? What?

00:03:55.541 --> 00:03:56.833
We took Deandre Ayton

00:03:56.833 --> 00:03:58.000
Oh, yeah

00:03:58.000 --> 00:03:59.208
How's he been this year?

00:03:59.208 --> 00:04:00.291
He’s actually pretty solid…

00:04:00.291 --> 00:04:01.000
Yeah?

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:03.166
Uh, yeah, he’s quietly having a decent squire season

00:04:03.166 --> 00:04:04.375
-Oh, that’s good to hear
-You like to hear that

00:04:04.375 --> 00:04:05.250
Ser Anthony Davis?

00:04:05.250 --> 00:04:07.625
You want to make a plea for House Pelicans?

00:04:07.625 --> 00:04:09.500
Yes

00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:13.125
Read this, and we will trade you to House Lakers

00:04:13.125 --> 00:04:14.666
Not that part. Don’t read that part!

00:04:14.666 --> 00:04:17.666
Ah, right. OK, let’s try this again

00:04:17.666 --> 00:04:20.791
We, House Pelicans, are but a humble house,

00:04:20.791 --> 00:04:23.458
and we kindly ask you for your blessing.

00:04:23.458 --> 00:04:26.875
Zion is the hero that House Pelicans needs,

00:04:26.875 --> 00:04:30.625
a knight who can take us further than one playoff series win...

00:04:30.625 --> 00:04:32.416
...in seven seasons.

00:04:32.416 --> 00:04:35.416
We once had a transformative, all-realm knight,

00:04:36.625 --> 00:04:39.000
but he lacked the fortitude to take… 

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:40.833
the fortitude it takes to commit to a small market.

00:04:40.833 --> 00:04:43.291
OK, it’s MY fault? That I—

00:04:43.291 --> 00:04:46.291
Sorry I couldn't beat House Warriors with Jrue Holiday

00:04:46.291 --> 00:04:48.333
and half a season of Boogie Cousins.

00:04:48.333 --> 00:04:50.750
Um, thank you, AD... 

00:04:50.750 --> 00:04:53.083
House Cavs, would you like to make your case?

00:04:53.083 --> 00:04:57.041
If the gods truly care to see the squire Zion flourish,

00:04:57.041 --> 00:05:00.041
they should give the first pick to House Cavs,

00:05:00.041 --> 00:05:03.541
where he will be surrounded by championship-caliber veterans

00:05:03.541 --> 00:05:05.125
and a Lord who knows how to win.

00:05:05.125 --> 00:05:09.083
Oh, please. You know, there’s a reason I left...

00:05:09.083 --> 00:05:09.708
twice.

00:05:09.708 --> 00:05:10.541
Oh yeah?

00:05:10.541 --> 00:05:12.250
Because you’ve made House Lakers such 

00:05:12.250 --> 00:05:14.250
a welcoming place for young talent?

00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:15.916
Who's fitting out now?

00:05:17.083 --> 00:05:18.000
Hey Kevin?

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:19.750
Yes, LeBron?

00:05:19.750 --> 00:05:20.875
I miss you.

00:05:20.875 --> 00:05:23.083
I...

00:05:23.083 --> 00:05:23.666
I miss you too

00:05:23.666 --> 00:05:24.791
All right, guys...

00:05:24.791 --> 00:05:27.791
let’s maybe keep the overt tampering to a minimum.

00:05:27.791 --> 00:05:29.500
OK, then. Who's next?

00:05:29.500 --> 00:05:30.291
House Hawks?

00:05:30.291 --> 00:05:32.708
Wait, every house here has to go? Ugh.

00:05:32.708 --> 00:05:36.000
Yes. House Hawks, please go ahead.

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:37.458
All right

00:05:37.458 --> 00:05:41.500
Um, dear lottery gods, our house is on the rise

00:05:41.500 --> 00:05:42.625
If Zion joins us—

00:05:42.625 --> 00:05:44.708
maybe 42-year-old Vince Carter

00:05:44.708 --> 00:05:47.000
won’t have to play 17 minutes a battle

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:49.208
OK, who else? Minnesota?

00:05:49.208 --> 00:05:50.541
I mean, how many No. 1 picks

00:05:50.541 --> 00:05:52.750
do you guys need to make the tournament?

00:05:52.750 --> 00:05:54.416
Apparently more than three

00:05:56.250 --> 00:05:57.041
This is fun

00:05:57.041 --> 00:05:58.083
Hey, do us

00:05:58.083 --> 00:05:58.541
No

00:05:59.291 --> 00:06:00.791
Who else? House Wizards?

00:06:00.791 --> 00:06:03.666
I mean, who wouldn’t want to play with Dwight Howard?

00:06:03.666 --> 00:06:04.291
By the way, 

00:06:04.291 --> 00:06:06.458
when does John Wall’s supermax start?

00:06:06.458 --> 00:06:07.583
Next year?

00:06:07.583 --> 00:06:09.041
Asking for a friend

00:06:09.041 --> 00:06:11.250
OK, who else we got? House Bulls?

00:06:11.250 --> 00:06:12.125
Oh yeah, I’m sure Zion wants

00:06:12.125 --> 00:06:14.125
to spend his first year having knights-only meetings

00:06:14.125 --> 00:06:16.375
-about how many push-ups are OK.
-OK. OK. All right. LeBron...

00:06:16.375 --> 00:06:17.541
please show a little respect.

00:06:17.541 --> 00:06:18.750
For many of these houses,

00:06:18.750 --> 00:06:20.541
this is the highlight of their season.

00:06:20.541 --> 00:06:21.958
Here, here! 

00:06:21.958 --> 00:06:24.291
Oh yeah, and why is that?

00:06:24.291 --> 00:06:26.083
Maybe instead of looking to the gods,

00:06:26.083 --> 00:06:28.000
you all should be looking at yourselves.

00:06:28.750 --> 00:06:31.916
Rubbish houses with uninspiring Lord Commanders,

00:06:31.916 --> 00:06:34.291
foolish masters of trade,

00:06:34.291 --> 00:06:35.375
arrogant lords

00:06:35.375 --> 00:06:36.250
You’re banned!

00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:37.500
These are things a knight, 

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:39.958
no matter how great, can't overcome.

00:06:39.958 --> 00:06:41.333
I learned that the hard way

00:06:41.333 --> 00:06:45.125
Zion may be the Prince who was Promised,

00:06:45.125 --> 00:06:47.125
but he will not save you.

00:06:47.125 --> 00:06:50.000
Because if you don’t give a GOAT the support he needs,

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:51.916
then he’s gonna walk out the door.

00:06:51.916 --> 00:06:54.208
and all you’re gonna be left with...

00:06:54.208 --> 00:06:56.041
...is poop on the floor.

00:06:56.041 --> 00:06:56.750
All right

00:06:56.750 --> 00:06:59.458
Well, on that note...

00:06:59.458 --> 00:07:02.791
why don't we go ahead and see who got the first pick?

00:07:02.791 --> 00:07:05.791
And the winner of the Zion lottery is...

00:07:05.791 --> 00:07:06.625
House Pelicans!

